# promise: #685
# Edge to edge with the toolbar hidden (the default), the page's top is all that stands in for the title bar: a drag
# there moved the window, but a double click did nothing (GitHub #685, neolytic, 0.1.54), where the strip above the
# card zooms it with the margin. Now a double click in the page's top 10 pt (the margin edge to edge takes away)
# zooms it as macOS is set to. The double click is a real one, through the window server (scripts/hid-click/click.m),
# 5 pt into the page's empty top.
requires screen
env CRA_TEST_BACKGROUND=0
budget rss=600 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false, "edgeToEdgeContent": true}
pace 0.5
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=zoom
wait 2
cra://debug?mainFrame=100,100,1000,700
wait 1
cra://debug?activate=1
wait 1
click page-top double
wait 2
cra://debug?toolbarZoom=page
expect-log toolbar zoom page: zoomed=1 grew=1
